Hi, I''m Steven — I build Memos. You''ve found the public demo: a real, living instance where you can poke at every feature before self-hosting your own.

Memos is an open-source, self-hosted home for short-form thoughts. Capture quickly, organize lightly, own everything.

> Most apps treat notes like documents. Memos treats them like thoughts — small, timestamped, searchable.

## Make yourself at home

- [ ] Scroll this Explore feed — everything here was written with Memos
- [ ] React to a memo you like (🎉 works great on this one)
- [ ] **Sign in** (top right) — SSO takes ten seconds and gives you your own space
- [ ] Write your first memo. One sentence is plenty. That''s the point.
- [ ] Like it? Star [the repo](https://github.com/usememos/memos) ⭐

🔒 *Psst — a few memos on this instance are hidden until you sign in. Members only.*

## What Memos can do

| Feature | Where to see it |
|---------|-----------------|
| **Markdown** | Everywhere — tables, `code`, task lists, quotes |
| **Math & diagrams** | KaTeX and Mermaid — see my rendering test memo |
| **Tags** | `#dev/git` — nested tags grow a tree in the sidebar |
| **Comments & reactions** | Right under this memo 👇 |
| **Memo references** | Alice''s weekly review links back to her week |
| **Attachments** | Ben''s golden-hour art from the coastal trail |
| **Locations** | Look for the 📍 pins |
| **Visibility** | Public, protected, or private — chosen per memo |

## Take it home

```bash
docker run -d -p 5230:5230 -v ~/.memos:/var/opt/memos neosmemo/memos:stable
```

